ÿØÿà␀JFIF␀␀␀d␀d␀␀ÿá8Exif␀␀MM␀*␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀In the Hertzprung-Russell diagram the temperatures of stars are plotted against their luminosities. The position of a star in the diagram provides information about its present stage and its mass. Stars that burn hydrogen into helium lie on the diagonal branch, the so-called main sequence. Red dwarfs like AB Doradus C lie in the cool and faint corner. AB Dor C has itself a temperature of about 3,000 degrees and a luminosity which is 0.2% that of the Sun. When a star exhausts all the hydrogen, it leaves the main sequence and becomes a red giant or a supergiant, depending on its mass (AB Doradus C will never leave the main sequence since it burns so little hydrogen). Stars with the mass of the Sun which have burnt all their fuel evolve finally into a white dwarf (left low corner).␀ÿáÊhttp://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/␀<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?> <x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/" x:xmptk="Exempi + XMP Core 5.6.0"> <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"> <rdf:Description rdf:about="" xmlns:avm="http://www.communicatingastronomy.org/avm/1.0/" xmlns:photoshop="http://ns.adobe.com/photoshop/1.0/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:Iptc4xmpCore="http://iptc.org/std/Iptc4xmpCore/1.0/xmlns/" xmlns:xmpRights="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/rights/" avm:PublisherID="eso" avm:ResourceID="eso0728c" avm:ResourceURL="https://www.eso.org/public/archives/images/original/eso0728c.tif" avm:ID="eso0728c" avm:MetadataVersion="1.1" avm:ReferenceURL="https://www.eso.org/public/images/eso0728c/" avm:Publisher="European Southern Observatory" avm:MetadataDate="2023-10-11T09:26:42.096140" avm:Type="Chart" photoshop:DateCreated="2007-06-19T00:00:00" photoshop:Source="European Southern Observatory" photoshop:Credit="ESO"> <avm:Spatial.ReferenceDimension> <rdf:Seq> <rdf:li>2662.0</rdf:li> <rdf:li>2652.0</rdf:li> </rdf:Seq> </avm:Spatial.ReferenceDimension> <avm:Subject.Category> <rdf:Bag> <rdf:li>E.3</rdf:li> </rdf:Bag> </avm:Subject.Category> <avm:Spatial.Notes> <rdf:Alt> <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default"/> </rdf:Alt> </avm:Spatial.Notes> <avm:Spectral.Notes> <rdf:Alt> <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default"/> </rdf:Alt> </avm:Spectral.Notes> <dc:description> <rdf:Alt> <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">In the Hertzprung-Russell diagram the temperatures of stars are plotted against their luminosities. The position of a star in the diagram provides information about its present stage and its mass. Stars that burn hydrogen into helium lie on the diagonal branch, the so-called main sequence. Red dwarfs like AB Doradus C lie in the cool and faint corner. AB Dor C has itself a temperature of about 3,000 degrees and a luminosity which is 0.2% that of the Sun. When a star exhausts all the hydrogen, it leaves the main sequence and becomes a red giant or a supergiant, depending on its mass (AB Doradus C will never leave the main sequence since it burns so little hydrogen). Stars with the mass of the Sun which have burnt all their fuel evolve finally into a white dwarf (left low corner).</rdf:li> </rdf:Alt> </dc:description> <dc:title> <rdf:Alt> <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Hertzsprung-Russell Diagram</rdf:li> </rdf:Alt> </dc:title> <dc:subject> <rdf:Bag> <rdf:li>Hertzsprungâ€“Russell diagram</rdf:li> <rdf:li> HR Diagram</rdf:li> <rdf:li>Stars</rdf:li> </rdf:Bag> </dc:subject> <Iptc4xmpCore:CreatorContactInfo Iptc4xmpCore:CiAdrPcode="D-85748" Iptc4xmpCore:CiAdrExtadr="Karl-Schwarzschild-Strasse 2" Iptc4xmpCore:CiUrlWork="http://www.eso.org/" Iptc4xmpCore:CiAdrCtry="Germany" Iptc4xmpCore:CiAdrCity="Garching bei MÃ¼nchen"/> <xmpRights:UsageTerms> <rdf:Alt> <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License</rdf:li> </rdf:Alt> </xmpRights:UsageTerms> </rdf:Description> </rdf:RDF> </x:xmpmeta>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 <?xpacket end="w"?>ÿí␀Photoshop 3.0␀8BIM␀␀␀␀ÇZ␀%G␀␀␀␀Hertzsprung-Russell Diagram␀Hertzsprungâ€“Russell diagram␀ HR Diagram␀Stars7␀20070619<␀000000n␀ESOs␀European Southern ObservatoryxIn the Hertzprung-Russell diagram the temperatures of stars are plotted against their luminosities. The position of a star in the diagram provides information about its present stage and its mass. Stars that burn hydrogen into helium lie on the diagonal branch, the so-called main sequence. Red dwarfs like AB Doradus C lie in the cool and faint corner. AB Dor C has itself a temperature of about 3,000 degrees and a luminosity which is 0.2% that of the Sun. When a star exhausts all the hydrogen, it leaves the main sequence and becomes a red giant or a supergiant, depending on its mass (AB Doradus C will never leave the main sequence since it burns so little hydrogen). Stars with the mass of the Sun which have burnt all their fuel evolve finally into a white dwarf (left low corner).␀8BIM%␀␀␀␀␀ByÐ³+
